{
  "label": "the source half of a move into a collection already holding the identity relocates, never deletes",
  "note": "Trash held the message under 3 before the move, so the move's create there is keyed by the identity minted over its provisional handle; the tombstone pairs with that create all the same, so the Remove relocates into Trash and carries no link_id, the copy Trash already held proving no delivery; INBOX holds no body, so nothing else could deliver the create, and a plain delete would take the only copy of the move (SYNC.md §3, §4, §5)",
